---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';

const quotes = [
  { text: 'We moved our incident process off spreadsheets in a week.', name: 'Grace Hopper', role: 'IT lead, Navy Labs' },
  { text: "Our customer portal runs on the same rules as the agents' workspace.", name: 'Alan Turing', role: 'Head of support, Bletchley' },
  { text: 'Self-hosting took one command and a coffee.', name: 'Katherine Johnson', role: 'Platform engineer' },
  { text: 'Access rules we can read in one place, at last.', name: 'Ada Lovelace', role: 'Security officer' },
  { text: 'Forms and lists for a new team took an afternoon.', name: 'Edsger Dijkstra', role: 'Business analyst' },
];
---

<p>
  <code>wc-carousel</code> shows its children as slides, for screenshots on a product page or a row
  of testimonials. Name what the slides are with <code>label</code>, and set
  <code>per-view</code> to show a few at once. The slides scroll with snap points, so swiping,
  trackpads and the scroll wheel work as they do anywhere else; the previous, next and picker buttons
  under them move a page at a time.
</p>
<p>
  A slide is never narrower than 15rem, so this carousel of three shows two, then one, as its
  container narrows. Slides out of view are <code>inert</code>, so Tab skips links the person cannot
  see. Before using a carousel, consider a grid: everything in it is visible at once, and nothing hides
  behind a button.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%;'>
    <wc-carousel id='carousel-demo' label='Testimonials' per-view='3'>
      {quotes.map(quote => (
        <figure style='margin: 0; padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 16px; background: var(--color-surface-container-low);'>
          <blockquote style='margin: 0 0 1rem;' class='text-body-large'>“{quote.text}”</blockquote>
          <figcaption class='text-body-small' style='color: var(--color-on-surface-variant);'>
            <b class='text-title-small' style='display: block; color: var(--color-on-surface);'>{quote.name}</b>
            {quote.role}
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </wc-carousel>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#carousel-demo').addEventListener('change', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('change: index ' + event.detail.index);
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
